{"page":"MAP3K7","gene":"MAP3K7","accession":"O43318","protein":"Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 7","length":606,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"O43318-1","name":"1B","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000369329.8"],"refseq":["NM_145331.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_663304.1"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-O43318-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-O43318-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":69,"plddt":[[0,23],[50,3],[70,2],[90,13],[70,3],[50,2],[70,3],[90,15],[70,13],[90,1],[70,3],[90,1],[70,1],[90,13],[70,2],[90,51],[70,1],[90,4],[70,2],[90,18],[70,2],[50,3],[0,1],[50,1],[0,7],[50,3],[70,2],[90,6],[70,7],[90,24],[70,12],[90,1],[70,2],[90,53],[70,3],[50,2],[0,39],[50,3],[0,2],[50,7],[0,142],[50,7],[70,1],[50,1],[70,41],[90,1],[70,2],[90,47],[70,6],[50,3],[0,1]]}},"features":[{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":300,"description":"Interaction with MAPK8IP1"},{"type":"Domain","start":36,"end":291,"description":"Protein kinase"},{"type":"Binding site","start":42,"end":50,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":63,"end":63,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":72,"end":72,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Active site","start":156,"end":156,"description":"Proton acceptor"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":158,"end":158,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":184,"end":184,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":184,"end":184,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by autocatalysis; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":187,"end":187,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":187,"end":187,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by autocatalysis; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":192,"end":192,"description":"Phosphoserine; by autocatalysis"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":209,"end":209,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":341,"end":341,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":367,"end":367,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":389,"end":389,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":439,"end":439,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":444,"end":444,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":446,"end":446,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":448,"end":448,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":455,"end":455,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":467,"end":467,"description":"(Microbial infection) O-acetylthreonine; by Yersinia YopJ; alternate"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Can form homodimer (PubMed:27426733). Binds both upstream activators and downstream substrates in multimolecular complexes. Interacts with TAB1/MAP3K7IP1, TAB2/MAP3K7IP2 and TAB3/MAP3K7IP3 (PubMed:10838074, PubMed:11460167, PubMed:12242293, PubMed:14670075, PubMed:16289117, PubMed:19675569, PubMed:8638164). Identified in the TRIKA2 complex composed of MAP3K7/TAK1, TAB1/MAP3K7IP1 and TAB2/MAP3K7IP2 (PubMed:11460167). Interacts with PPM1L and PPM1B/PP2CB (PubMed:11104763). Interaction with PP2A and PPP6C leads to its repressed activity (PubMed:17079228). Interacts with TRAF6 and TAB1/MAP3K7IP1; during IL-1 signaling (PubMed:10094049, PubMed:12242293). Interacts with TAOK1 and TAOK2; interaction with TAOK2 interferes with MAP3K7 interaction with IKKA, thus preventing NF-kappa-B activation (PubMed:16893890). Interacts with DYNC2I2 (via WD domains) (PubMed:19521662). Interacts with CYLD and RBCK1 (PubMed:17449468, PubMed:17548520). Interacts with TGFBR1; induces MAP3K7/TAK1 activation by TRAF6 (PubMed:18758450). Interacts with MAPK8IP1 and SMAD6 (By similarity). Interacts with isoform 1 of VRK2 (PubMed:18286207). Interacts with DAB2; the interaction is induced by TGF-beta stimulation and may mediate TGF-beta stimulated JNK activation (PubMed:15894542). Interacts with TRIM5 (PubMed:21512573). Part of a complex containing ITCH, NDFIP1 and MAP3K7 (By similarity). Interacts with IFIT5; the interaction synergizes the recruitment of IKK to MAP3K7 and enhances IKK phosphorylation (PubMed:26334375). Interacts with PLEKHM1 (via N- and C-terminus) (By similarity). Interacts with TRIM8 (PubMed:22084099). Found in a complex with SH3RF1, RAC2, MAP2K7/MKK7, MAPK8IP1/JIP1, MAPK8/JNK1 and MAPK9/JNK2 (By similarity). Interacts with SASH1 (PubMed:23776175). Interacts with RIPK1 (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with herpes simplex virus 2 protein US2; this interaction induces MAP3K7 phosphorylation and subsequent activation"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"O43318-2","name":"1A","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":579,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000369332.7","ENST00000700580.1"],"refseq":["NM_003188.4"],"refseqProteins":["NP_003179.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":["ENST00000700580.1"],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,403],[404,431,176]],"edits":[{"start":404,"end":430,"original":"AYSKPKRGHRKTASFGNILDVPEIVIS","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":27,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-O43318-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-O43318-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":72.1,"plddt":[[0,23],[50,3],[70,2],[90,13],[70,3],[50,2],[70,3],[90,15],[70,13],[90,1],[70,3],[90,